Comments:
    Identical to helical-MHDTurb, except that io_hdf5 is used (and we use mpicomm since nompicomm does not work with hdf5_io_parallel).
    The purpose is to test whether the Python routines in pc.read work with HDF5 simulations.
    
    I have also removed the lzero_spec_zerok to get the sample to work on my somewhat older development branch.
    
    For unknown reasons, the 2D averages (yaver and zaver) do not match those in the helical-MHDTurb sample. The current reference data are the same as in the standard (nohdf5, nompicomm) sample, and thus this test currently fails (running script tests).
    Notes
        The outputs for io_dist+mpicomm are the same as io_dist+nompicomm, so it looks like the introduction of HDF5 is somehow changing the results (but only of the 2D (yaver, zaver) averages).
        The read_data.py test (which reads var.aa) passes even with hdf5+mpicomm, so the difference cannot even be attributed to different random seeds for the initial conditions.
        By inserting print statements in io_hdf5.f90/output_average_2D, I can see that the expected values are there in the local_data pointer array.
            This suggests the issue is in the output_hdf5 (output_hdf5_slice_2D) subroutine
